    "question": {
      ":question/id": "1c834df5-8f8d-5d8a-a914-3f5aa984dbc7",
      ":question/problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{24}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 3\\csc^{2}(6 x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "If we let $u=6 x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=6\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{6}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives\n\n| $x$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{24}$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{12}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ | $\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{24}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{12}} 3\\csc^{2}(6 x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} 3\\csc^{2}(u)\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\csc^{2}(u)\\,\\text{d}u \\\\ & =- \\frac{1}{2}\\cot(u)\\big|_{\\frac{\\pi}{4}}^{\\frac{\\pi}{2}} \\\\ & =- \\frac{1}{2}(\\cot(\\frac{\\pi}{2})-\\cot(\\frac{\\pi}{4})) \\\\ & =- \\frac{1}{2}(0-1) \\\\ & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "7fb06030-2a0a-55bc-840a-51b14dacc2a1",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
